<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves to banking system.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves to banking system.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to add  reserves to the banking system via a round of over the weekend repurchase  agreements on Friday.</p>
<p>Carol Stone, economist at Nomura Securities, saw an add need of $6  to $7 billion through the remainder of the maintenance period.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
